<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1920 CE · capital Vladikavkaz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived state of the North Caucasus mountain peoples, declared in 1918 amid the collapse of the Russian Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917, a congress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-united-mountaineers-of-the-north-caucasus-and-dagestan">Union of United Mountaineers of the North Caucasus and Dagestan</a>, bringing together <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingush-people">Ingush</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabardians">Kabardians</a>, Dagestanis and others. In May 1918 it declared independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> with the support of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was led by a government of the mountaineer elite under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tapa-chermoev">Tapa Chermoev</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pshemakho-kotsev">Pshemakho Kotsev</a>, and aimed at a federal, democratic state. It never controlled its territory firmly: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/terek-cossack-host">Terek Cossacks</a> and local leaders contested it, and its seat moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buynaksk">Temir-Khan-Shura</a> and elsewhere. It had a constitution and envoys abroad.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1919 the White army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a> occupied much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> and dissolved the government. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>'s victory in 1920, the Soviets created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mountain-autonomous-soviet-socialist-republic">Mountain Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</a> in 1921.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus.jpg" alt="Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus" width="320" height="188"><figcaption>Image: Arsenekoumyk · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Mountain_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vladikavkaz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tapa Chermoev, Pshemakho Kotsev</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam; Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian; various Caucasian languages</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mountain Republic, Republic of the Mountaineers of the North Caucasus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus" aria-label="Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5758 650 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6078 906L6078 906M6078 906L5635 424M6078 906L6611 554M6078 906L5820 533M6078 906L6113 908"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6078 906h0M5635 424h0M6611 554h0M5820 533h0M6113 908h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6078 906h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6078 906h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vladikavkaz. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
